(4261770, 610583, 39830, '<td valign="top">Actually only the furthest two lenses are Tamron glass. The first in line is my Canon 50mm, and the second is the wife''s (<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=53781" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">photomouse</a>) Sigma 28-135mm. Tamron is not my favorite lens maker, but the title was just in pun. I was hoping that the uniqueness of my shot (aswirl in a pool of flower shots) might counteract the lack of flair, but oh well. I am still very pleased with the shot. I think I am really starting to grow as a photographer, and this site has had a lot to do with that. I thank all of you who commented and voted on my image. (Of course I think you 2 voters might want to seek out a good optometrist.)</td>', 'Actually only the furthest two lenses are Tamron glass. The first in line is my Canon 50mm, and the second is the wife''s ( photomouse) Sigma 28-135mm. Tamron is not my favorite lens maker, but the title was just in pun. I was hoping that the uniqueness of my shot (aswirl in a pool of flower shots) might counteract the lack of flair, but oh well. I am still very pleased with the shot. I think I am really starting to grow as a photographer, and this site has had a lot to do with that. I thank all of you who commented and voted on my image. (Of course I think you 2 voters might want to seek out a good optometrist.)', '2007-11-21 00:11:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4261781, 611656, 66384, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon. This is a gorgeous image -- really awesome.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon. This is a gorgeous image -- really awesome.', '2007-11-21 00:14:06.000000', NULL, 0),
